<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">8 January in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 8 January, from 871 to 1959.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">871 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,155 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Æthelred I and Alfred defeat the Danes at Ashdown</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aethelred-i-of-wessex">Æthelred I of Wessex</a> and his brother Alfred led the West <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxons</a> to victory over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-heathen-army">Great Heathen Army</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danes">Danes</a> at Ashdown, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berkshire">Berkshire</a> Downs. The Danish king Bagsecg and five earls were killed.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ashdown">Battle of Ashdown</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aethelred-i-of-wessex">Æthelred I of Wessex</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfred-the-great">Alfred the Great</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1198">1198 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">828 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Lotario dei Conti di Segni is elected Pope Innocent III</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Cardinal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-innocent-iii">Lotario dei Conti di Segni</a> was elected pope after the death of Celestine III and took the name Innocent III. He went on to reassert papal rule over central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and launch the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fourth-crusade">Fourth Crusade</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-innocent-iii">Pope Innocent III</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1297">1297 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">729 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">François Grimaldi seizes the fortress of Monaco</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Disguised as a Franciscan friar, the Genoese Guelph <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francois-grimaldi">François Grimaldi</a> talked his way into the Rock of Monaco and took it. His descendants, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-grimaldi">House of Grimaldi</a>, still rule the principality.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1815">1815 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">211 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Andrew Jackson defeats the British at New Orleans</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Jackson's mixed force repulsed a British assault on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-orleans">New Orleans</a>, inflicting some 2,000 casualties. Fought after the Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghent">Ghent</a> was signed but before news arrived, it made Jackson a national hero.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1918">1918 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">108 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Woodrow Wilson presents his Fourteen Points</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Addressing Congress, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/woodrow-wilson">President Wilson</a> outlined a peace programme including open diplomacy, free seas, self-determination and a league of nations. It framed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armistice-of-11-november-1918">armistice</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris-peace-conference-1919-1920">Paris Peace Conference</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fourteen-points">Fourteen Points</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/woodrow-wilson">Woodrow Wilson</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-saud" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ibn-saud.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1926">1926 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">100 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Abdulaziz ibn Saud proclaimed King of the Hejaz</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After conquering <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medina">Medina</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/najd">Nejd</a> was proclaimed King of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hejaz">Hejaz</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/masjid-al-haram">Great Mosque of Mecca</a>. In 1932 he merged his realms into the Kingdom of Saudi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medina">Medina</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hejaz">Hejaz</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1940">1940 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">86 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Britain introduces food rationing</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Bacon, butter and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> became the first foods rationed in wartime <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>. Rationing extended to most foods during the war and did not end entirely until 1954.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1959">1959 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">67 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Charles de Gaulle takes office as President of France</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-de-gaulle">De Gaulle</a> became the first President of the Fifth Republic, whose constitution greatly strengthened the executive. He governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> until 1969, ending the war in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a> in 1962.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-de-gaulle">Charles de Gaulle</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algeria">Algeria</a></div></div></li></ol>
